          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1f401fe057529b79b8f5c938b142d5f6c02399c46cfc7b7bf415b0615493b439:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/roles.py#L30-L91",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b5a5f0627c68402c82669caf4c80ae4d23419220538dd5861b9331a62c5b2f41:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_88af0306276d41509330725c5affbb95",
      "statement": "The permission matrix is deny-by-default with glob scopes: PermissionMatrix.check returns False for missing actions, allow False entries, non-dict input, and resources that fail fnmatch against the entry scopes, while an empty scope list or '*' scope allows any resource for a granted action and a grant/revoke are audited edits under a lock.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/permissions.py#L33-L100",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:46af50fa96666e7db14591658d2ffa5efd6dd11f6a650ed791b9d742edc5aa53:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1a9383977660430885b397bee46d7fb0",
      "statement": "A server accepts task_requests only after an ordered gate: relationship status accepted (else FRIEND_NOT_FOUND), permission plus resource scope (else PERMISSION_DENIED), then a token-bucket rate limit consuming one token from the per-(friend, action) bucket and one from the friend's global bucket (else transient RATE_LIMITED with retry_after); only then is the executor invoked, so permission-denied requests never consume tokens or model cost.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/rate_limiter.py#L109-L131",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:60a8cd863187af658856f65e3a643a87a94665528efd043d20a6b60ed851de49:"
        },
