    {
      "id": "claim_9c4dd118c3d743abb7a33b29172b39a2",
      "statement": "Errors carry a short stable ASCII code and no internal detail: error envelopes are themselves signed and shaped as payload with error_code, detail, and in_reply_to_nonce, detail strings are truncated (200 chars on the wire, 120 chars in rejection audit entries), RATE_LIMITED, TRANSPORT_ERROR, and TASK_LIMIT_REACHED are flagged transient with retry_after, and unknown inbound codes degrade to a generic HAAPError on the client.",
