    {
      "id": "claim_33245adfa9c84d1c82856e4183d59381",
      "statement": "Blocking is deny at the point of use rather than a router-level drop: Directory.public_keys intentionally keeps blocked entries so their signatures still verify, the task path then fails the accepted-status requirement, marketplace traffic from blocked senders is rejected with PERMISSION_DENIED, the client refuses new outbound friendships toward blocked fingerprints (FriendBlockedError), and because bootstrap messages are exempt from friendship checks a blocked agent can re-initiate a handshake that again lands in the owner's policy/human decision.",
      "evidence": [
